; ── The embedded Go runtime, as a virtual library ─────────────────────────────
; emit_go.ml copies the runtime (runtime/go/teslrt) into every emitted project from
; Embedded_go_runtime.files, an OCaml literal generated by gen/gen_go_runtime.ml.
; The OCaml linker includes any compilation unit a linked module references, so a
; plain module here would ride along into EVERY executable that links the compiler
; library — including the js_of_ocaml browser playground, whose 2 MB artifact ceiling
; it broke (1.13 MB → 2.37 MB: the Go sources as JavaScript string literals).
;
; A virtual library separates the interface (embedded_go_runtime.mli, here) from its
; implementation:
;   embedded/  the real snapshot, promoted from runtime/go/teslrt — the DEFAULT, so
;              bin/main.exe and every test link it without naming it;
;   none/      `files = []`, which playground/dune selects explicitly.  The playground
;              only type-checks and lints; it never writes a Go project.
(library
 (name tesl_go_runtime)
 (wrapped false)
 (virtual_modules embedded_go_runtime)
 (default_implementation tesl_go_runtime_embedded))
